# /etc/fstab — mos A/B layout (read-only squashfs + dm-verity root).
#
# Rendered from os/boards/cx3576/board.env by os/rootfs/build.sh; the at-sign
# placeholders are partition GUIDs from that file. Never edit this on device:
# the whole tree is on a verity-protected read-only squashfs.
#
# The root filesystem is deliberately absent. The kernel assembles /dev/dm-0
# from dm-mod.create= on the cmdline and mounts it read-only; there is no
# remount to perform and no entry that could ever succeed in rewriting it.
#
# Storage tiers (docs/design/ro-root.md section 4):
#   /srv        DATA       application data. Precious, GROWS to fill the disk.
#   /mnt/state  STATE      configuration + identity. Precious, small.
#   /mnt/meta   META       update/appliance metadata. Precious, small.
#   /var        EPHEMERAL  disposable runtime residue. Fixed size, wipeable.
# Only /srv carries x-systemd.growfs: it is the only partition repart grows.
#
# PARTUUID values are lowercase because udev's /dev/disk/by-partuuid/ symlinks
# are created from libblkid's lowercase GUID formatting, and systemd's
# fstab-generator resolves PARTUUID= through those symlinks verbatim.
#
# <device>                      <mount>     <type>  <options>                   <dump> <pass>
@SRV_LINE@
PARTUUID=@STATE_GUID@           /mnt/state  ext4    noatime                     0      2
PARTUUID=@META_GUID@            /mnt/meta   ext4    noatime                     0      2
PARTUUID=@EPHEMERAL_GUID@       /var        ext4    @VAR_OPTS@                  0      2
tmpfs                           /tmp        tmpfs   noatime,nosuid,nodev,mode=1777 0   0
